# Copy to .env in the repo root. The AWS lines are required: task up, the infra and the deploy scripts fail without them.
# Docker Compose also uses defaults in compose.yaml.

# --- Credentials and region: the same names locally (here) and in CI (GitHub environment). ---
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test
# Prod CI sets AWS_REGION and either AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID + AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY or AWS_ROLE_ARN + AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE (OIDC).
# Never commit real keys.

# Published host port (the compose stack is Floci only). Its container port is 4566.
# FLOCI_PORT=11566
# Experiment KPI replay workers in the backtest job (Go, CPU bound). Unset = one per CPU.
# EXPERIMENT_SIM_WORKERS=
# Experiments run on the C++ engine. Each experiment can set its own "Parallel processes" in the create form
# (stored as experiment.parallelism). EXPERIMENT_CPP_PROCESSES is only the fallback when an experiment has no
# value (unset = one per CPU). The largest value the API accepts is the CPU count of the Experiment API process
# (the Lambda), or EXPERIMENT_MAX_PARALLELISM when set. The max instances per C++ process default to 500.
# EXPERIMENT_CPP_PROCESSES=
# EXPERIMENT_MAX_PARALLELISM=
# EXPERIMENT_CPP_SHARD_MAX=500
# CPP_SMA_CROSS_BIN=/usr/local/bin/strategy-sma-cross   # the experiment engine (C++, always) needs it for ma-cross; set in the dagobert-backtest image
# CPP_SIGNAL_CONSENSUS_BIN=/usr/local/bin/strategy-signal-consensus   # same for signal-consensus
# Ingest market-data provider id (default binance). One provider per ingest run.
# INGEST_PROVIDER=binance

# --- Floci / serverless migration (steps 1–5) ---
# After: task infra:local  (terraform apply against Floci)
# DEPLOY_ENV=local
# LAKE_BUCKET=dagobert-local-lake
# EXPERIMENT_ARTIFACTS=fs
# Set EXPERIMENT_ARTIFACTS=s3 to dual-write/read instance report.json via Floci S3.
#
# Step 4 / 14 — experiment catalog is Postgres when DATABASE_URL is set.
# Experiment catalog is Postgres when DATABASE_URL is set, otherwise SQLite.
# There is no DynamoDB experiment catalog.
#
# Candle parquet lake (Go jobs). Compose defaults to s3 (Floci bucket); fs keeps ./data/parquet.
# LAKE_BACKEND=fs        # fs (default) | s3; the Floci Lambdas and ECS tasks get s3 from Terraform
# LAKE_DUAL_WRITE=0      # 1 to also upload to S3 while LAKE_BACKEND=fs
# LAKE_BACKEND also places experiment shards and the prepare cache (experiments/<id>/...) in the bucket.
# Existing ./data/parquet lake: task lake:upload
#
# Experiment fan-out runs on Step Functions and the worker Lambda. Terraform sets EXPERIMENT_SFN_ARN and
# EXPERIMENT_BATCH_SIZE on the Lambdas (infra/terraform/experiment_*.tf); nothing is set here.
#
# Control plane: Aurora PostgreSQL on Floci (Terraform: task infra:local; Atlas migrations in db/):
# POSTGRES_USER=trading
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=trading
# POSTGRES_DB=trading
# Host tools (task db:migrate) use 127.0.0.1:7001 when DATABASE_URL is unset.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://trading:trading@127.0.0.1:7001/trading?sslmode=require&search_path=public
# Apply: task db:migrate
# The Vite dev server forwards /tradingcopilot.v1.* to the Floci API Gateway: task frontend:dev sets
# VITE_DEV_API_PROXY and VITE_DEV_API_PREFIX from scripts/local-api-url.sh.
# Diff after HCL edits: task db:diff name=my_change
